<%# ** THE EDIT SCREEN FOR AN ACCOUNT'S OPENING RECORD (account-openings §2; fix round round 2 —
    items 1 and 2). ** An opening entry is an ordinary row in the user's history — it has to be
    findable and deletable there, which is what puts the question back on the account's card — but
    almost nothing about it may be CHANGED from here, because the record is two rows that have to
    move together: the entry and the transfer `AccountOpening` writes beside it.

    ** WHAT IS READ-ONLY, AND WHY EACH ONE IS. **

      THE ACCOUNT — re-pointing it called `Entry#route_income_to!`, which rewrote the transfer onto
      another account: measured, an Ally corrected to $1,000 afterwards showed $500 while HYSA
      silently held the difference.
      THE AMOUNT — it IS the opening figure, and changing it has to recompute the transfer.
      `amount: 0` passed validation (zero is legal for an opening row) and then raised a 500 against
      `account_movements`' own `amount > 0` CHECK, AFTER the real movement had been deleted.
      THE CATEGORY AND THE ITEM — they are the app's, not the user's: `Opening Balance` or
      `Opening Shortfall` by the sign of the figure, and one `Initial balance` item under each.

    ** AND THAT IS WHY THIS IS ITS OWN PARTIAL RATHER THAN FOUR BRANCHES INSIDE `_form`. ** The big
    form binds three Stimulus controllers — `app--entry--form` (the two TomSelects),
    `app--entry--impact` (the envelope card) and `app--entry--routing` (the "Lands in" toggle) — and
    every one of them reaches for a target that is not on the page once the controls above are
    read-only. `app--entry--routing#categoryChanged` threw "Missing target" on the first branch of
    this fix for exactly that reason. A form with no editable pickers needs no controller at all, so
    this one binds none.

    WHAT IS STILL EDITABLE: the date and the description. Neither is part of the arithmetic, and a
    user who wants to annotate the row their setup wrote is entitled to.

    Local: `entry` (the opening Entry). %>
<%= simple_form_for(entry) do |f| %>
  <%= f.error_notification %>
  <%= hidden_field_tag :previous_url, @previous_url if @previous_url.present? %>

  <div class="bg-white shadow-sm rounded overflow-hidden border border-gray-100 mb-6"
       data-opening-entry="<%= entry.opening_account.name %>">
    <div class="p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Opening balance</h2>

      <%# THE SENTENCE AND ITS DOOR — `Entry#opening_line` and `Entry::OPENING_DOOR` are the one
          spelling, shared with the 422 `EntriesController#update` answers a crafted PATCH with. %>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-5" data-opening-line>
        <%= entry.opening_line %> ·
        <%= link_to Entry::OPENING_DOOR, root_path, class: "text-status-info hover:underline" %>
      </p>

      <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-5">
        <div>
          <dt class="form-label">Category</dt>
          <dd class="text-sm text-gray-900"><%= entry.category.name %></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="form-label">Name</dt>
          <dd class="text-sm text-gray-900"><%= entry.item.name %></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="form-label">Amount</dt>
          <dd class="text-sm text-gray-900 tabular-nums"><%= number_to_currency(entry.amount) %></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="form-label">Lands in</dt>
          <dd class="text-sm text-gray-900"><%= entry.opening_account.name %></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <%= f.input :date,
          as: :string,
          hint: "The day this account started at this figure.",
          input_html: { type: "date", value: entry.date&.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") } %>

      <%= f.input :description,
          wrapper_html: { class: "mt-5" },
          placeholder: "Add any notes about this record",
          hint: "Optional details about this entry",
          input_html: { rows: 3 } %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:justify-end gap-3">
    <%= link_to "Cancel", (@previous_url.presence || entries_path), class: "btn btn-secondary" %>
    <%= f.button :submit, "Update Entry" %>
  </div>
<% end %>
